      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the perimeter of the triangle. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a triangle with sides \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nP = a + b + c\n\\]\n\nGiven the sides of the triangle are \\( 6.1 \\) cm, \\( 8.2 \\) cm, and \\( 9.7 \\) cm, we can calculate the perimeter as follows:\n\n\\[\nP = 6.1 + 8.2 + 9.7 = 24 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nSince the square and the triangle have equal perimeters, the perimeter of the square is also \\( 24 \\) cm. Let the side length of the square be \\( s \\). The perimeter \\( P \\) of a square is given by:\n\n\\[\nP = 4s\n\\]\n\nSetting the perimeter of the square equal to the perimeter of the triangle, we have:\n\n\\[\n4s = 24\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( s \\):\n\n\\[\ns = \\frac{24}{4} = 6 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of a square is given by the square of its side length:\n\n\\[\nA = s^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the side length \\( s = 6 \\) cm:\n\n\\[\nA = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ square centimeters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36}\n\\]",
