    "text": "To find the area of the square, we first need to determine the perimeter of the triangle. The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of the lengths of its three sides. Given the side lengths of the triangle are 6.1 cm, 8.2 cm, and 9.7 cm, we can calculate the perimeter as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter of the triangle} = 6.1 + 8.2 + 9.7 = 24 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nSince the square and the triangle have equal perimeters, the perimeter of the square is also 24 cm. The perimeter of a square is given by four times the length of one of its sides. Let the side length of the square be \\( s \\). Then, we have:\n\n\\[\n4s = 24\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( s \\), we get:\n\n\\[\ns = \\frac{24}{4} = 6 \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThe area of a square is given by the square of its side length. Therefore, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area of the square} = s^2 = 6^2 = 36 \\text{ cm}^2\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{36}\\).",
